## V64 package (userspace wakelock counter; boot V63 + system) [HARDWARE: PASS]
# V63 showed that late_resume correctly reactivates sprdfb, mip4 and touchkey, but the Android 10
# system-suspend service kept writing mem every 100 ms. On kernel 3.10 each write
# reactivates early_suspend, producing an intermittent screen. V64 changes SystemSuspend to
# mUseSuspendCounter=true: while PowerManagerService.Display is held the thread stays
# blocked and cannot undo the resume. Keeps keylayout V62 and boot V63. Exact AP:
# boot.img + system.img.
e4641a1672e610aab448bb666678b43981116f271b2c373b9042ab14534fbf38  boot.img (V63, -> KERNEL)
75f7d8f769168340ccf1e1db43aece0f4b07566911e405e15824b08d7fce7eb5  android.system.suspend@1.0-service (V64)
4d7ca49c63142f02e2f5d09a6b50609d1f99b7a86120321b0f7da705f28bdb8b  system-legacy-sparse-odin-v64.img (-> SYSTEM)
297209ae12cd9061ee100518ab1aaba587e34071de5859016f941a19244b13f6 *sm-t280-phase6/packages/SM-T280-android10-suspend-counter-PHASE6-v64-DO-NOT-FLASH.tar.md5

## V63 package (full late_resume; boot-only) [HARDWARE: OSCILLATION; integrated in V64]
# V62 resolved the POWER mapping: physical press powers off (Awake->Asleep, Display OFF) and wakes
# Android (WAKE_REASON_POWER_BUTTON, Display ON). On wake, V61 only reactivated sprdfb:
# `late_resume: call handlers` did not appear, mip4 stayed Disabled and the DISPC ended in
# `BIT_DISPC0_EB still set`; screen visible but frozen and without touch events. V63 changes
# the V61 deferred worker to call request_suspend_state(PM_SUSPEND_ON), running the
# full late_resume in reverse order (LCD, mip4, touchkey and the rest). ONLY boot.img; system V62
# is not touched. Package verified with exact boot.img content.
