## V59-SYSFIX package (power button: FINAL FIX - permanent wakelock; boot 3328bd1e + NEW system 5d9b5de3)
# AP boot+system (~970MB). KEY: the device is SYSTEM-AS-ROOT -> / is mounted from the
# SYSTEM partition (ext4), and /init.board.rc LIVES IN system.img, NOT in the boot ramdisk. That is why the
# previous attempts (boot-only and boot+old-system) did NOT change /init.board.rc (still 10084 without
# wakelock): they reused the V58 system. This package carries the system REBUILT with
# init.board.rc = 10381 (verified by debugfs: contains "gtex_power_wake"). The wakelock is
# acquired in 'on boot' -> the system does NOT enter mem-suspend -> the power key wakes the
# powered-off screen. SELinux Permissive -> init writes the node. Trade-off: worse standby.
# boot V59 (3328bd1e) = ramdisk with the rc too (irrelevant at runtime due to system-as-root)
# + V58 light_sleep_en=0. Previous HW test (runtime wakelock "mywake"): IRQ 56->66, Display ON.
3328bd1e45dce6e340704a6b665d33e30a0993377567779511c0644e311fcc62  boot.img (V59, -> KERNEL)
5d9b5de32ea24ed0f46e2759c4d488f8a1027f2f156c9d70747f57f5ed140c3f  system-legacy-sparse-odin-v59.img (init.board.rc 10381 + wakelock, -> SYSTEM)
4a9dee80af252b3137723c7b387540099098d2973a8c5f08999a88be76ec117c *sm-t280-phase6/packages/SM-T280-android10-powerkey-wakelock-PHASE6-v59-SYSFIX-DO-NOT-FLASH.tar.md5

## V58 candidate package (power button: FIX THAT WORKS - light_sleep off; NEW boot 6645e743)
# EMPIRICALLY CONFIRMED: the cause was SPRD's LIGHT-SLEEP (cpuidle-scx35,
# light_sleep_en=1) which pauses the AP subsystem (incl. ADI/PMIC) on screen-off -> the
# power IRQ (analog EIC) does not wake. With light_sleep_en=0 (runtime) IRQ 422
# increments and the tablet WAKES on pressing POWER. V58 sets light_sleep_en=0 by default in
# drivers/platform/sprd/cpuidle-scx35.c. TRADE-OFF: worse standby. NEW boot:
# boot_sha256=6645e743db1a72c41c16a57a789594ed8a1a94222ae9db9467990888cbca7ad7. Includes
# V55(sw video)+V56+V57. sprdwl.ko unchanged (WiFi remains). See KNOWN-ISSUES P1.
02e3c3936c57bb401020a27631704553a91b03b70c991710923ad747dd31456b *sm-t280-phase6/packages/SM-T280-android10-powerkey-lightsleep-PHASE6-v58-DO-NOT-FLASH.tar.md5

## V57 package (power button: irqchip EIC set_wake; KERNEL -> boot 7bb45c35) [Linux ready, insufficient alone; see V58]
# V56 (enable_irq_wake in sci_keypad_suspend) was not enough: power is the "irq-a-eic
# powerkey" IRQ (analog EIC of the PMIC) and its irqchip a_eic_irq_chip in drivers/gpio/gpio-eic.c
# had NO .irq_set_wake -> enable_irq_wake(422) gave -ENXIO -> the wake was not armed. V57
# adds .irq_set_wake = sci_gpio_irq_set_wake to a_eic_irq_chip and d_eic_irq_chip. With V56+V57
# POWER wakes from suspend. KERNEL -> NEW boot:
# boot_sha256=7bb45c35abe254dbcb6ecc0a3fd57e8f659b54a23ed5dc4a0d39cfcde6a98d5f. sprdwl.ko
# unchanged (WiFi remains). Includes V55 (sw video + low_ram).
d30d60fc939d768f5b42f121433fa3ebca868fb4b19d2b8edbfc00ddf9a59861 *sm-t280-phase6/packages/SM-T280-android10-powerkey-eic-PHASE6-v57-DO-NOT-FLASH.tar.md5

## V56 package (power button: wake from suspend; KERNEL -> NEW boot 5f23247b) [insufficient; see V57]
# V55 (POWER WAKE keylayout) was not enough: the sc_keypad.c driver had an EMPTY
# sci_keypad_suspend() -> it did not arm enable_irq_wake for the power IRQ (EIC) -> no wake from
# suspend. V56 adds enable_irq_wake(gpio_to_irq(PB_INT)) in suspend / disable in resume.
# KERNEL CHANGE: the zImage relink was forced (the build did not detect it on its own) and
# sprdwl.ko was rebuilt/copied (identical vermagic -> WiFi remains). NEW boot:
# boot_sha256=5f23247b887906f6da00b148b3769bcbb8b72fa8c632c723e666c5d0ab1a4b25.
# GRAPHICS PENDING (performance): the display is capped at ~8fps GLOBAL (UI and video)
# because the SPRD HWC composes via GPU (CLIENT) and DUMPS via CPU (memcpy in fb_post) to the
# framebuffer -> compositor at 84% CPU, ~100ms/frame. It does not use DISPC overlays or the
# GSP blitter. Optimization pending from phase 5 (it ended up working, not fast). See
# results/fase-6/graphics-8fps-DIAGNOSIS.md.
98e44089bf655afbe7787aad32d3e2fd107f13eadbb3d5deaf4df68cb0e6ef60 *sm-t280-phase6/packages/SM-T280-android10-powerkey-PHASE6-v56-DO-NOT-FLASH.tar.md5

